DentalRecords - Design
======================

DATA
----
familyArray : String[familySize]
    One name per family member.

teethRecord : char[familySize][2][]
    Plane  = person (same index as familyArray)
    Row 0  = uppers (UPPER), Row 1 = lowers (LOWER)
    Column = one tooth: 'I' incisor, 'B' bicuspid, 'M' missing
    Rows    : each row's length is that layer's number of teeth.

ALGORITHM
---------
main method
    Print the welcome banner
    Read the family size
    While the size is < 1 or > MAX_PEOPLE
        Print error, read the size again
    Create familyArray and teethRecord for that many people
    For each family member
        Read the name into familyArray
        Read the upper and lower for that member
    Do
        Read a menu option (converted to lower case)
        While the option is not p, e, r or x
            Print error, read the option again
        If p: printRecord
        If e: extractCommand
        If r: rootCommand
    While the option is not x
    Print the exit message with a smile

teethRecorder
    Read a tooth string (converted to upper case)
    While the string has an invalid letter (validateType) or more than MAX_TEETH teeth
        If it has an invalid letter: print "Invalid teeth types"
        Otherwise: print "Too many teeth"
        Read the string again
    Return the string as an array of characters

validType
    For each character in the string
        If it is not I, B or M, return false
    Return true

printRecord
    For each family member
        Print the name
        For each layer (upper then lowers)
            Print the layer label
            For each tooth in the layer
                Print the tooth number and its letter

extractCommand
    Read a name and find its position with findMember
    While the position is -1
        Print error, read the name again
    Read a layer letter (converted to lower case)
    While the letter is not u or l
        Print error, read the letter again
    Convert the letter to the row index (UPPER or LOWER)
    Read a tooth number
    While the number is < 1, > the number of teeth in the row,
          or that tooth is already missing
        If the number is out of range: print "Invalid tooth number"
        Otherwise: print "Missing tooth"
        Read the number again
    Set that tooth to M (Missing)

findMember
    For each family member
        If the name matches, ignoring case, return the index
    Return -1

rootCommand
    Set the incisor, bicuspid and missing counts to 0
    For each family member, for each layer, for each tooth
        Add 1 to the count for that tooth's type
    If there are incisors
        discriminant = sqrt(B*B + 4*I*M)
        Print root 1 = (-B + discriminant) / (2*I)
        Print root 2 = (-B - discriminant) / (2*I)
    Else if there are bicuspids
        Print the single root M / B
    Else
        Print that there are no roots